  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_de522482334d446aa2bd5392886ed38e",
      "statement": "step oauth implements OAuth 2.0/OIDC authorization at the command line and doubles as the backend for OIDC provisioners; CA commands obtain OIDC tokens by re-executing step oauth rather than linking the OAuth code.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L79-L307",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:abe51b4b8d8edf15995efd48431f82b1276dc94e2553014b4ec555b47ba06d04:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_generator.go#L144-L169",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b8fc1a4ae7b27158b6d8bb033718a63281a9afe422fc46eac7a4db4b19ffd47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_763cf73747a440e1b48ed7a047043ed3",
      "statement": "oauthCmd selects one of four flows: loopback authorization (default), Device Authorization Grant (--console or --console-flow device), out-of-band manual authorization (--console-flow oob), or JWT bearer/two-legged via --account service accounts, with a hidden implicit flow requiring --insecure and --client-id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L351-L513",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25db8cf4d3da23dcf7b30016ba2921009c6160f7371638c0ad95ed30cf4d0af0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0f93b071a9e94ed7898696f27ce74223",
      "statement": "The Device Authorization Grant polls the token endpoint at the provider-given interval (default 5 seconds) until completion or expiry (default 5-minute window), preferring verification_uri_complete when provided and accommodating Google's non-spec verification_url field.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L861-L952",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:001b18ef620d5830152c65cd4fc2699a106b198993972600be3c2b9a07aa218c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91403d780b4247858192460c6181b698",
      "statement": "Loopback authorization starts a local HTTP server — --listen fixes the address/port and --listen-url overrides the advertised redirect_uri — opens the browser (or prints the URL when STEP_OPEN_BROWSER=0), and times out after 2 minutes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L729-L814",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f2b8e12c6ee72155e7834acfbef6418518f1d3d1e46894c68ca20bdca4562607:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_98f46fcfdc54432a81e3199a1e51ed2d",
      "statement": "Service-account flows sign an RS256 JWT assertion with the account's private key and exchange it via the urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer grant; with --jwt the self-generated JWT is returned directly as the token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L981-L1088",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:868bfbd210df6e44f44dadeaa0594e8505db189f233ad6ba65fa61184e115b40:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_150ea0f8e638460d95eb04d0a147cdde",
      "statement": "Google and GitHub are hardcoded knownProviders; other providers must be https OIDC discovery URLs unless explicit --authorization-endpoint (or --device-authorization-endpoint) and --token-endpoint flags are given, each requiring the token endpoint companion.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L410-L428",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44d707ac95de279ce0ebeefff63837b3dc8d34e6309affd078769f59ed72f2bc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L573-L586",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4927c0bf42e4dadf0b17563e2f3ef9f81f34427850660914cfa8a6ca54c6d63a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L632-L656",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eda34d6b9408a7775b9337fb391cc5c0b9c052860ff93e15bd7f8c2bcac83072:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1bc814b519494fe2a05125516abf0275",
      "statement": "Default client credentials are the published Google installed-app client ID/secret (documented in-source as having no security access), with a separate default pair for the device flow.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L35-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3646e486dc494801a843d26eb8b126fd694e75798b86ad9200e245977a30b81:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53596a5590484a98a76620fe438d8703",
      "statement": "The authorization request uses PKCE S256 with a SHA-256 of a 64-character alphanumeric challenge, a random state, a 256-bit nonce, login_hint from --email, and --prompt/--auth-param extensions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1197-L1231",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52b5f48922465ee9e7a2109c23c0937f753b206bf2ddf6dbb2436dd8b07b72cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_998902e5bef74de58f9ab7956820d371",
      "statement": "The callback handler validates state before exchanging the authorization code, supports a terminal redirect page via --redirect-url, and returns a failure page pushing the error into errCh on provider errors or mismatched state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1092-L1150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d0d5bec3ee3f964a03d9a4cef5a5ff845ec238f2dd2920f6facdcb12314c12b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L1292-L1324",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:153afa856e95ecadf59bc50cc2040a210e341c3a72331f58f3e98411ea567c41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_65d00afb7cde42e5af31e6769edd0012",
      "statement": "Output modes: --header prints 'Authorization: Bearer <token>', --bare prints only the token (ID token with --oidc, otherwise access token), and the default prints the full token JSON.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/oauth/cmd.go#L515-L537",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ca9f6ec1b6aa3b1c66bee241a4364eec2a3decbedad4e265158b579a8767b7b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_05d80d199c7148189cd5f7bcbfdc1843",
      "statement": "generateOIDCToken executes 'step oauth --oidc --bare --provider <config-endpoint> --client-id ... --client-secret ...' via exec.Step, appending scopes, auth params, --console when requested, and --listen from the provisioner's ListenAddress unless STEP_LISTEN is set; trimmed stdout becomes the OIDC token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://exec/exec.go#L130-L149",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d597e001cb81774f6c36c9f6034ba38838fb05450fb6481b83eb96fd0e206aaf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_generator.go#L144-L169",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b8fc1a4ae7b27158b6d8bb033718a63281a9afe422fc46eac7a4db4b19ffd47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84e324eb1cf44c9c8787348dd2599b26",
      "statement": "Users can invoke the same pattern directly: step ca certificate --token $(step oauth --oidc --bare) <subject> ... is a documented example.",
